# This repository stores line endings exactly as committed (core.autocrlf=false) and its files
# legitimately mix CRLF and LF, often within the same file. Without this, `git diff --check` reports
# every CRLF line as "trailing whitespace" — hundreds of false positives on any sizeable change,
# which hides the real ones. `cr-at-eol` tells Git the carriage return belongs there; genuine
# trailing spaces and tabs are still reported.
#
# Deliberately NOT setting `text`/`eol` here: normalising endings would rewrite nearly every file and
# bury real changes under whole-file diffs.
* whitespace=cr-at-eol
